WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:06.694
This is a quick guide to recording a respirator fit test in the ENVSS Field app on a
Chromebook.

2
00:00:06.704 --> 00:00:11.670
You'll need the job number, and a photo of the PortaCount fit test report.

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.538
The job and names in this video are example data.

4
00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:22.618
Sign in with your ENVSS Google account as usual, then click the job on the Projects
screen.

5
00:00:22.628 --> 00:00:27.123
We're using job 0 0 1 9 3 8 9.

6
00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:30.058
Click New project event.

7
00:00:30.068 --> 00:00:36.006
Under Event type, choose Respirator fit testing, check the date, and click Create
event.

8
00:00:42.244 --> 00:00:47.650
The app numbers it for you: the job number, then FIT, then 0 0 1.

9
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.480
The next fit-testing event on this job will be FIT 0 0 2.

10
00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:58.512
Now click Add individual report, and choose the photo of the TSI report.

11
00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:01.108
On a phone this opens the camera.

12
00:01:01.118 --> 00:01:04.498
On the Chromebook, pick the photo from Files.

13
00:01:04.508 --> 00:01:08.487
Get the whole report in the shot, flat and in focus.

14
00:01:09.157 --> 00:01:12.208
The app reads the photo with Google Vision.

15
00:01:12.218 --> 00:01:15.788
Give it a few seconds, and stay on this screen.

16
00:01:16.466 --> 00:01:18.856
Next is the confirm screen.

17
00:01:18.866 --> 00:01:30.091
The photo is on the left, and the fields from the report are filled in on the right:
the ID number, name, company, test and due dates, the PortaCount serial number, and
the respirator.

18
00:01:32.587 --> 00:01:40.806
Scroll down to check the protocol, pass level, the four exercises, the overall fit
factor, and the PASS or FAIL result.

19
00:01:40.816 --> 00:01:44.255
Anything the app isn't sure about is highlighted.

20
00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:48.727
Check every field against the photo, and fix anything that's wrong.

21
00:01:48.837 --> 00:01:55.613
The person who was tested still needs to sign; your ENVSS sign-off is filled in from
your sign-in.

22
00:01:56.225 --> 00:02:01.090
If you can't get the person's signature straight away, click Save without signing.

23
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:06.209
You'll get an unsigned PDF, and you can open the report later to sign it.

24
00:02:06.885 --> 00:02:11.378
Otherwise, when everything's correct, click Continue to signature.

25
00:02:12.408 --> 00:02:23.511
Your ENVSS sign-off is filled in automatically from your Google sign-in: your name,
your envss.com.au email, and the date and time in AWST.

26
00:02:23.521 --> 00:02:25.757
You do not need to sign.

27
00:02:26.461 --> 00:02:31.951
Hand the device to the person who was tested, and they sign in the Person tested box.

28
00:02:31.961 --> 00:02:34.906
Use Clear if you need to start again.

29
00:02:36.043 --> 00:02:38.577
Click Save signed PDF.

30
00:02:39.223 --> 00:02:50.206
The app makes a one page PDF in the TSI report layout, with the ENVSS header, your
electronic sign-off, and the individual's signature, and downloads a copy.

31
00:02:50.216 --> 00:02:55.180
It's named by surname, first name, mask model and test date.

32
00:02:55.757 --> 00:02:59.192
Back on the event, the report shows as signed.

33
00:02:59.202 --> 00:03:07.245
Under Files for Drive, the PDF is copied as a new file into the Fit-Tests folder in
the job's Field App Drive folder.

34
00:03:07.255 --> 00:03:10.837
Nothing already in the job folder is changed.

35
00:03:11.515 --> 00:03:14.530
Add a report for each person you test.

36
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.436
When everyone has signed, click Mark event complete.

37
00:03:18.446 --> 00:03:23.770
If you need this guide again, there's a How to link at the bottom of every fit-testing
event.

